WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.530
A desert at sunset.

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:07.450
"Two vast and trunkless legs
of stone" stand in the sand.

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.300
Nearby, half sunk, a shattered face.

4
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:14.730
On the pedestal, words
appear in the stone.

5
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:19.440
"My name is Ozymandias, king
of kings: Look on my works,

6
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.190
ye Mighty, and despair!"

7
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:27.390
A king ordered those words cut
in stone, over 3,000 years ago.

8
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.010
So who has the last word now?

9
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.180
In this mission, you'll find out
who is really telling this story.

10
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:38.340
You'll look again at that broken face,
and what the sculptor read in it.

11
00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:41.640
And you'll find the
moment the sonnet turns:

12
00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.160
"Nothing beside remains."

13
00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.480
Your mission: decide
who has the last word.
